                <pb facs="0876" n="762" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg762"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">724.3415/1420: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Culbertson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-10-10T19:00:00-04:00">October 10, 1931—7
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 9:40 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>127. I explained today to the Minister for Foreign Affairs the situation set
                    forth in the Department’s telegram 47, October 9, 6 p.m.<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d621-f1"/> He said that he had been using his influence to persuade
                    Bolivia and Paraguay to submit their dispute to the neutral commission and that
                    on the basis of the information which I gave him he would renew his efforts
                    along the lines indicated especially through his Minister in La Paz. He
                    expressed sincere appreciation of your efforts to settle the dispute and offers
                    his fullest cooperation.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Culbertson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
